{%- comment -%}
  The one "does this product need the dog's name before it can be made?"
  test, shared by the buy box (name field, no dynamic checkout), product
  cards (never a one-tap add) and the Bed Finder (its Add opens the product
  instead of adding a bed without the name).

  Personalised when:
    - the custom.personalisation_label metafield is set; or
    - its product type contains "Personalis" / "Personaliz"; or
    - a tag equals personalised, personalized, personalised dog bed,
      personalized dog bed or personalisation:yes.
  Tag personalisation:no turns it off whatever else says so.

  Output: the word "true" when personalised, nothing otherwise. Capture it:
    {%- capture is_pers -%}{%- render 'personalised', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if is_pers == 'true' -%} … {%- endif -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if product != blank
    assign ps_tags = product.tags | join: '|' | downcase | prepend: '|' | append: '|'
    assign ps_type = product.type | default: '' | downcase
    assign ps_label = product.metafields.custom.personalisation_label.value | default: '' | strip
    assign ps_on = false
    if ps_label != '' or ps_type contains 'personalis' or ps_type contains 'personaliz'
      assign ps_on = true
    elsif ps_tags contains '|personalised|' or ps_tags contains '|personalized|' or ps_tags contains '|personalisation:yes|'
      assign ps_on = true
    elsif ps_tags contains '|personalised dog bed|' or ps_tags contains '|personalized dog bed|'
      assign ps_on = true
    endif
    if ps_tags contains '|personalisation:no|'
      assign ps_on = false
    endif
    if ps_on
      echo 'true'
    endif
  endif
-%}
